.TH supersede 1  "supersede " 
.SH NAME
supersede \- Supersede an existing knowledge element with a new replacement element
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsupersede\fR <\fB\-\-title\fR> [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIEXISTING_ELEMENT_ID\fR> <\fIREPLACEMENT_TYPE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Supersede an existing knowledge element with a new replacement element
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Title for the replacement element
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Optional detailed description for the replacement element
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIEXISTING_ELEMENT_ID\fR>
Existing element ID (UUID) to supersede
.TP
<\fIREPLACEMENT_TYPE\fR>
Replacement element type (e.g. requirement, design\-decision)
